@X0BPPLC 1.0 was released with PCBoard 15.0.  At the time, any PPE would run under
15.0, but none would run under any previous version.  Since then, New versions
of PCB and new versions of PPLC have been released, and some PPEs will run
under Some versions, but not others.
 
The reason that these updated versions of PCB are required is because the code
that executes when a PPE instructs it to is actually code INSIDE the PCBoard
executable file.
 
The chart below indicates which versions of PCBoard are required to run PPEs
which were compiled with the corresponding PPLC version.
 
 
@X0APPL     PCBOARD VERSION REQUIRED
----    ------------------------
@X0E1.0     15.0
2.0     15.1
3.0     15.2
3.01    15.2
3.1     15.21
3.2     15.22/15.23
3.3     15.3
